{"c":[{"id":"def92aca321a0958","sum":"CC 2.1.302 hooks expand \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}\" from env (safe); skill text is pasted raw. sr-initialize owner: default plugin dirs by path; else claude if <copy root>/data/<id> or installed_plugins.json lists it, dev if stockroom-inline, cursor via CURSOR_PLUGIN_ROOT, else ask.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261017T135752Z-8f76ec9421650d2c","text":"Claude Code 2.1.302 shell-form hooks: \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}\" is expanded by the shell from the env, not pasted as text (a $ in the path survives), so hooks/claude-hooks.json is safe from path re-parsing. Skill text is pasted raw.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261017T143558Z-05746a642d0f531d","text":"sr-initialize Step 2 owner (round 3): default plugins dirs by path; elsewhere a cache-shaped copy is claude if Claude's data dir is <copy root>/data/<id> or installed_plugins.json lists it, dev if data dir is stockroom-inline, cursor via CURSOR_PLUGIN_ROOT, else ask.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"ed3458896fa1f4ac","sum":"sr-initialize Step 2 reads ${CLAUDE_SKILL_DIR}/${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_DATA} from a quoted heredoc (IFS= read -r); a value still starting with $ was not substituted. Paths in shell text are quoted (shlex.quote, Makefile \"...\"): space and ' work; $, backtick, \", \\, % out of scope.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261017T143616Z-2bbea48021b44381","text":"sr-initialize Step 2 now reads ${CLAUDE_SKILL_DIR} and ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_DATA} from a quoted heredoc (IFS= read -r), so the shell never parses the pasted paths and no env var stands in; a value still starting with $ was not substituted. Supersedes the SKILL_DIR=\"...\" note.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261018T171632Z-1ff8e252c90ac5da","text":"Every path stockroom writes into shell text is quoted: Step 2 heredoc, shim and scheduler entries via shlex.quote, Makefile recipes via double quotes. A space or ' must work; rarer chars ($, backtick, \", \\, %) are out of scope (2026-10-18).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
